    "content": "<p>Ask carpet importers in London, New York, Sydney or Dubai where handmade rugs come from, and a large share will give the same answer: Bhadohi. This small city in Uttar Pradesh, together with neighbouring Mirzapur, forms what is widely recognised as the largest hand-knotted carpet-producing region in the world. This article explains how that happened, how the industry works and what it means for international buyers. It is written by Tajmahal Products, a sixth-generation family manufacturer based on Chauri Road, Bhadohi.</p>\n<h2>Where is Bhadohi?</h2>\n<p>Bhadohi is a district headquarters in eastern Uttar Pradesh, between Varanasi and Prayagraj (Allahabad), close to the Ganga. Together with Mirzapur, it forms a carpet belt that has produced handmade rugs for generations. The area is often called the \"carpet city\" of India, and many export houses and weaving communities are concentrated here.</p>\n<h2>A brief history</h2>\n<p>The carpet tradition of this region is usually traced to the Mughal era, when weavers skilled in Persian techniques settled in northern India. Local tradition holds that weavers moved to the area during the Mughal period and gradually built a craft community around it. Whatever the exact origins, by the twentieth century the region had developed into a major centre of production and, increasingly, of export.</p>\n<p>Carpet making is often passed down inside families. Knowledge of dyeing, weaving, finishing and design is learned from a young age, and many of today's leading manufacturers have family histories of several generations in the trade. At Tajmahal Products, our family's association with weaving spans over a century and six generations, and we entered the international export market in 1967.</p>\n<h2>Why one region became a world centre</h2>\n<h3>A complete supply chain in one place</h3>\n<p>Carpet making involves many specialised steps: wool sourcing, spinning, dyeing, weaving, washing, clipping, finishing, packing and export documentation. In Bhadohi almost every one of these has an established ecosystem of skilled workers and suppliers within a short distance. That shortens lead times and makes sampling and customisation easier.</p>\n<h3>Depth of skill</h3>\n<p>Generations of weavers, designers, dyers and finishers keep traditional techniques alive. This accumulated skill is hard to reproduce elsewhere quickly.</p>\n<h3>Range of constructions</h3>\n<p>The region produces hand-knotted carpets, hand-tufted rugs, handwoven flatweaves and more. A buyer can often source an entire collection from a single area.</p>\n<h3>Flexibility</h3>\n<p>Manufacturers can adapt designs, sizes, colours and materials for each customer, which suits retailers, designers and hospitality projects.</p>\n<h2>What Bhadohi produces</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Hand-knotted carpets</strong> in Persian-inspired, Mughal, tribal and contemporary designs.</li><li><strong>Hand-tufted rugs</strong> for scale, consistency and modern styles.</li><li><strong>Handwoven rugs and flatweaves</strong> such as dhurries.</li><li><strong>Gabbeh, Kazak, Moroccan and other style families</strong> produced as custom or catalogue ranges.</li></ul>\n<p>Our own portfolio, for example, includes six signature collections: Gabbeh, Kazzak, Tufted, Moroccan, Mughal and Mughal Super.</p>\n<h2>The role of trade bodies</h2>\n<p>The Indian carpet industry is supported by trade associations and export promotion bodies. The Carpet Export Promotion Council (CEPC), headquartered in New Delhi, promotes carpet exports, and the All India Carpet Manufacturers Association in Bhadohi represents manufacturers. These bodies organise trade fairs, set industry priorities and help buyers and sellers connect. Our late founder, Haji Jalil Ahmad Ansari, served as Honorary Secretary of the All India Carpet Manufacturers Association, Bhadohi for four consecutive years, as President of the All India Carpet Trade Fair Committee for six consecutive years, and as an elected member of the CEPC Committee of Administration for over 18 years.</p>\n<h2>Who buys from Bhadohi</h2>\n<p>Buyers include rug retailers, wholesalers, importers, interior designers, hotel and hospitality developers and private-label brands. Major markets include North America, Europe, Australia and the Middle East, all of which Tajmahal Products serves.</p>\n<h2>Challenges and how good manufacturers handle them</h2>\n<p>Like every craft industry, carpet making faces challenges: keeping skills alive across generations, maintaining consistent quality at volume, ethical labour standards and rising material costs. Responsible manufacturers address these through quality-control systems, fair business practices, transparent sampling and certifications.</p>\n<h2>How to evaluate a Bhadohi supplier</h2>\n<ol><li>Confirm whether they manufacture directly or trade through intermediaries.</li><li>Ask about export experience, markets served and credentials such as export house status and export council membership.</li><li>Review samples carefully before approving bulk orders.</li><li>Ask about quality-control steps.</li><li>Check communication quality: clear answers, quick replies, honest timelines.</li></ol>\n<h2>Visiting Bhadohi</h2>\n<p>Many buyers visit workshops and showrooms in person. Arranging a visit gives you a chance to see looms in action, meet weavers and review sample ranges. Varanasi is the nearest major airport and rail hub for most visitors.</p>\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n<h3>Why is Bhadohi called the carpet city of India?</h3>\n<p>Because it is the centre of a large, long-established handmade carpet industry, with a concentration of weavers, dyers, finishers and exporters.</p>\n<h3>Are all Bhadohi carpets hand-knotted?</h3>\n<p>No. The region makes hand-knotted, hand-tufted and handwoven carpets. A good supplier will tell you clearly which construction you are buying.</p>\n<h3>Can I buy directly from a manufacturer in Bhadohi?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Many manufacturers, including Tajmahal Products, work directly with importers, retailers and designers.</p>\n<div class=\"blog-cta\"><p><strong>Looking for handmade rugs from Bhadohi, India?</strong> Tajmahal Products is a sixth-generation, family-owned manufacturer and exporter of handmade carpets and rugs, established 1967. For custom and private-label enquiries, email <a href=\"mailto:tmproducts.bhadohi@gmail.com\">tmproducts.bhadohi@gmail.com</a> or call +91 82995 01435.</p></div>",
