    "category": "Export & Sourcing",
    "readTime": "10 min",
    "wordCount": 1310,
    "publishedAt": "2026-11-25",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What is the standard HS code for hand-knotted wool carpets?",
        "a": "Hand-knotted wool carpets are classified under HS Code 5701.10, while hand-tufted rugs fall under 5703.10."
      },
      {
        "q": "What shipping documents are required to import rugs from India?",
        "a": "Commercial Invoice, Packing List, Bill of Lading / Air Waybill, Certificate of Origin (COO), and Fumigation / Phytosanitary Certificate."
      },
      {
        "q": "Which Indian ports handle rug shipments from Bhadohi?",
        "a": "Air freight operates via New Delhi (DEL) or Varanasi (VNS). Ocean containers ship via Inland Container Depots (ICD Madhosingh / ICD Kanpur) connected to Nhava Sheva (JNPT) or Mundra."
      }
    ],
    "content": "<p>Importing handmade carpets from India offers unmatched pricing, bespoke customization, and access to generational artistry. However, successful commercial importing requires navigating customs protocols, shipping logistics, and mandatory export documents. This comprehensive checklist from Tajmahal Products ensures smooth clearance at overseas customs.</p>\n<h2>Essential Export Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Commercial Invoice & Detailed Packing List:</strong> Itemizing bale numbers, dimensions in cm/inches, net/gross weights, knot densities, and material breakdown.</li>\n  <li><strong>Certificate of Origin (COO):</strong> Issued by the Carpet Export Promotion Council (CEPC) or Chamber of Commerce to claim preferential tariff agreements under GSP or bilateral trade treaties.</li>\n  <li><strong>Bill of Lading (Ocean) or Air Waybill (Air):</strong> Documenting carrier custody, consignee details, and notify party.</li>\n  <li><strong>Fumigation and Pest Inspection Certificate:</strong> Ensuring natural wool bales comply with ISPM-15 biosecurity standards.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Air Freight vs. Sea Freight Comparison</h2>\n<p>For urgent hospitality orders or bespoke luxury rugs under 500 kg, international air freight provides door-to-door transit in 5-8 business days. For volume container shipments (20ft / 40ft FCL), ocean freight via ICD Madhosingh delivers the lowest cost per square meter over a 25-35 day transit window.</p>\n<h2>Export Packaging Standards</h2>\n<p>Each rug is rolled tightly pile-inward around rigid PVC or bamboo cores, wrapped in high-density waterproof polythene, and encased in heavy-duty cross-stitched hessian jute sacking with tamper-evident heat seals.</p>\n<div class=\"blog-cta\"><p><strong>Looking for handmade rugs from Bhadohi, India?</strong> Tajmahal Products is a sixth-generation, family-owned manufacturer and exporter of handmade carpets and rugs, established 1967. For custom and private-label enquiries, email <a href=\"mailto:tmproducts.bhadohi@gmail.com\">tmproducts.bhadohi@gmail.com</a> or call +91 82995 01435.</p></div>",
