    "category": "Pillar Guides",
    "readTime": "12 min",
    "wordCount": 1640,
    "publishedAt": "2026-12-05",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What does Warp and Weft mean?",
        "a": "Warp refers to the longitudinal vertical foundation yarns strung tightly on the loom; weft refers to the horizontal yarns woven across to lock the knots in place."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is a Boteh motif?",
        "a": "A tear-drop or pinecone motif of ancient Persian origin, representing eternal life and sprouting seeds, known internationally as Paisley."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is the difference between Ghiordes and Senneh knots?",
        "a": "Ghiordes is a symmetrical double-wrap knot popular in tribal rugs; Senneh is an asymmetrical single-loop knot allowing finer curvilinear lines."
      }
    ],
    "content": "<p>Navigating the rich vocabulary of handmade carpets can feel like learning an ancient secret code. This comprehensive A-to-Z glossary compiled by Tajmahal Products defines the fundamental weaving terms used by master artisans, auction houses, and interior designers worldwide.</p>\n<h2>A</h2>\n<p><strong>Abrash:</strong> Natural, subtle color striations across a carpet resulting from variations in dye lots or handspun wool spinning density.</p>\n<p><strong>All-Over Pattern:</strong> A repetitive design field lacking a central focal medallion, ideal for versatile furniture placement.</p>\n<h2>B</h2>\n<p><strong>Boteh:</strong> The iconic teardrop or droplet motif symbolizing fertility, life, and rebirth, ancestral to the modern Paisley pattern.</p>\n<p><strong>Border:</strong> The decorative frame enclosing the carpet's central field, consisting of a main primary border flanked by guard stripes.</p>\n<h2>C</h2>\n<p><strong>Carding:</strong> The mechanical or hand combing process that untangles raw fleece into aligned, parallel wool fibers ready for spinning.</p>\n<p><strong>Clipping (Embossing):</strong> Hand trimming using angled artisan shears along design outlines to create high-relief textural dimension.</p>\n<h2>K</h2>\n<p><strong>KPSI:</strong> Knots Per Square Inch, the gold standard unit for measuring knot density in hand-knotted textiles.</p>\n<p><strong>Kilim:</strong> A flat-woven tapestry rug produced by tightly interweaving colored wefts through warps without a raised pile.</p>\n<h2>W</h2>\n<p><strong>Warp:</strong> The structural vertical threads stretched under high tension between the loom's top and bottom beams.</p>\n<p><strong>Weft:</strong> Horizontal passes of yarn shot between rows of knots to structurally bind the pile.</p>\n<div class=\"blog-cta\"><p><strong>Looking for handmade rugs from Bhadohi, India?</strong> Tajmahal Products is a sixth-generation, family-owned manufacturer and exporter of handmade carpets and rugs, established 1967. For custom and private-label enquiries, email <a href=\"mailto:tmproducts.bhadohi@gmail.com\">tmproducts.bhadohi@gmail.com</a> or call +91 82995 01435.</p></div>",
