    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Can a hole in a hand-knotted carpet be rewoven?",
        "a": "Yes. A master restorer reconstructs the vertical warp foundation and reties individual knots using color-matched vintage wool."
      },
      {
        "q": "What should I do if the fringe begins to unravel?",
        "a": "Secure the area immediately with an overcast stitch or hand binding to prevent loss of the knot foundation."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is antique rug restoration cost-effective?",
        "a": "For authentic hand-knotted heirlooms, professional restoration preserves and often elevates market appraisal value."
      }
    ],
    "content": "<p>Unlike machine-made carpets bound with latex glue that crumbles with age, genuine hand-knotted carpets possess remarkable structural resilience. Every part of a knotted rug, from edge selvedges to central warps, can be dismantled, restrung, re-knotted, and restored to pristine condition by skilled craftsmen.</p>\n<h2>Common Structural Issues and Solutions</h2>\n<h3>1. Unraveling Fringes (End Loss)</h3>\n<p>The fringe of a hand-knotted rug consists of exposed warp ends. If end stop-stitches fail, rows of knots can slide free. Artisans re-anchor the warp ends using invisible Zubaida knots or hand-overcasting.</p>\n<h3>2. Side Selvedge Wear</h3>\n<p>The outer edges (selvedges) take the brunt of foot traffic and vacuum roller contact. Re-binding the edge with matching double-corded wool secures the structural perimeter.</p>\n<h3>3. Moth Damage Reweaving</h3>\n<p>Moth larvae feed on natural wool keratin in dark, undisturbed areas under sofas. Restoration experts clean the damaged zone, splice in fresh cotton warps, and re-knot each missing motif knot with precision.</p>\n<div class=\"blog-cta\"><p><strong>Looking for handmade rugs from Bhadohi, India?</strong> Tajmahal Products is a sixth-generation, family-owned manufacturer and exporter of handmade carpets and rugs, established 1967. For custom and private-label enquiries, email <a href=\"mailto:tmproducts.bhadohi@gmail.com\">tmproducts.bhadohi@gmail.com</a> or call +91 82995 01435.</p></div>",
